// WHY: `return 5` from a `-> number errors` function. The return type is
// `Type::ErrorsCapable{ inner: Number }`, so the shared int-literal→number gate's
// `matches!(expected_ty, Type::Number{..})` was FALSE through the wrapper and the
// return-site consumer fell through to the GENERIC mismatch instead of the
// teaching error. Pre-fix RED signature (fix-loop round 4):
//   `return` produces `int`, but this function must return `number errors`.
// Post-fix: the SAME teaching error the plain `-> number` return emits
// (`Write it as a decimal literal: 5.0`), routed through the one shared gate
// after unwrapping the ErrorsCapable wrapper.
function toll() -> number errors {
  return 5
}

function entrypoint() -> nothing {
  print(`unreachable`)
}
